  <prompt>
    Move every customer stamp's Redis from Azure Cache for Redis with an access key to Azure Managed Redis Balanced_B0
    (high availability on, Microsoft Entra only), and make the BFF and the L2 Worker able to connect to an Entra-only cache
    with their user-assigned managed identity, so no Redis key or connection string exists for a stamp.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer (Bicep, .NET 10 BFF + L2 control plane, StackExchange.Redis). Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `customer.bicep` deploys a `Microsoft.Cache/redisEnterprise` Balanced_B0 cluster with HA, one database with access keys
    disabled and an access-policy assignment for the stamp UAMI, and outputs its endpoint (host:10000) — no key, no
    connection string, no Key Vault secret. H2a carries the endpoint to H4b, which sets it as a plain BFF app setting. The
    BFF (and the L2 Worker's idempotency cache) connect with `Microsoft.Azure.StackExchangeRedis`
    `ConfigureForAzureWithUserAssignedManagedIdentityAsync(clientId)` over RESP3 whenever an endpoint is configured; a
    connection string is accepted only outside Azure (Development/Testing). H1 registers `Microsoft.Cache`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner D12 (2026-09-30, researcher `redis-per-customer-stamp-amr-decision-2026-09-30.md`): Azure Cache for Redis
      Basic/Standard/Premium retires 2028-09-30 and new-customer creation is blocked since 2026-04-01; per-customer Redis is
      Azure Managed Redis `Balanced_B0`, HA on, Entra only, stamp UAMI via access-policy assignment (API 2025-07-01, OSS
      clustering, AllKeysLRU). D13: keyless stamps. Today (inventory 2026-10-04): `modules/redis.bicep:72`
      `Microsoft.Cache/redis@2023-08-01`, outputs `redisPrimaryKey` (:98) and `redisConnectionString` (:100) from
      `listKeys()`; `customer.bicep:472-482` calls it without the UAMI, `:638-641` sets `Redis__ConnectionString` as a KV
      reference, `:781` puts the connection string into `kvSecretValues`; manifest `Redis-ConnectionString` (:244-263,
      from-bicep-output, app settings `ConnectionStrings__Redis` + `Redis__ConnectionString`). BFF `CacheModule.cs:59-97`
      reads only a connection string and connects synchronously; pub/sub users (`JobStatusService`,
      `MembershipCacheInvalidator/Subscriber`) need RESP3 so the token refresh can re-AUTH the subscription connection;
      SCAN loops over `GetEndPoints()` (`ChatContextMappingService.cs:154-174`, `MembershipCacheInvalidationSubscriber.cs:280-294`)
      must stay cluster-safe under OSS clustering. Resolved StackExchange.Redis is 2.7.27; `Microsoft.Azure.StackExchangeRedis`
      3.3.1 needs ≥ 2.10.1. The Worker (`Dispatch/DispatchModule.cs:156-165`) uses the per-env platform cache with a connection
      string — T242b recreates the dev one Entra-only, so the Worker needs the same managed-identity path. H1's default
      provider list (`SubscriptionReadinessOptions.cs:33-64`) omits `Microsoft.Cache`.
    </background>
