  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D12">
      Stamp cache: `Microsoft.Cache/redisEnterprise@2025-07-01`, sku `Balanced_B0`, `highAvailability: 'Enabled'`,
      `minimumTlsVersion: '1.2'`, `publicNetworkAccess` set explicitly; one database `default`: `clusteringPolicy:
      'OSSCluster'`, `evictionPolicy: 'AllKeysLRU'`, `accessKeysAuthentication: 'Disabled'` (explicit), port 10000;
      `databases/accessPolicyAssignments` with `accessPolicyName: 'default'` and `user.objectId` = the stamp UAMI
      principalId. HA and SKU become parameters (dev T242b uses B0 non-HA through the per-env bicepparam), defaults = D12.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="D13 + ADR-028 A4">
      No `listKeys()`, no key or connection-string output, no `Redis-ConnectionString` secret for stamps, no
      `Redis__ConnectionString` / `ConnectionStrings__Redis` stamp app setting. The endpoint is a plain app setting
      (`Redis__Endpoint` = `{host}:10000`). In the BFF and the Worker, when `Redis:Endpoint` is set the client authenticates
      only with its user-assigned managed identity (client id from the existing `ManagedIdentity:ClientId` /
      `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` setting — no new identity setting) over RESP3; a connection string is used only when no endpoint is
      set AND the environment is Development or Testing. Outside Development/Testing a connection string without an endpoint
      fails at startup with a message naming `Redis__Endpoint`.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 (BFF hot path)">
      Placement Justification in the POML notes; publish size measured against a FRESH master build from short paths
      (Compress-Archive, both file counts reported); `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` shows no new
      HIGH; `CacheModuleTests` updated; ADR-032 symmetric registration kept (the Redis-off branches unchanged).
      `/conflict-check` at start (BFF entry/DI hot path).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010 / CLAUDE.md §11">
      No new interface, no new options class: extend `RedisOptions` with `Endpoint`. One shared helper for "build an
      Entra-authenticated multiplexer" is allowed only if BFF and Worker can both reference it without a new project
      reference; otherwise each module configures its own.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">
      Per-env platform caches are NOT recreated here (T242b, live, owner approval). `infrastructure/byok/main.bicep`,
      `vnet.bicep`'s `snet-redis`, `alerts.bicep`, `Rotate-RedisKey.ps1`, `redis-key-rotation.yml`, `Deploy-RedisCache.ps1`
      and `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` are untouched (they serve the per-env caches — T242b decides them); list them in the
      notes. No change to cache keys, TTLs or the `spaarke:` instance prefix.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The `Microsoft.Cache/redisEnterprise` 2025-07-01 schema in the installed Bicep types lacks `accessKeysAuthentication` or `accessPolicyAssignments` → STOP and report (do not fall back to keys or a preview API without owner approval).</trigger>
    <trigger>The package bump (StackExchange.Redis ≥ 2.10.1, `Microsoft.Azure.StackExchangeRedis`) adds a HIGH CVE, a pre-release dependency, or ≥ +5 MB publish size → STOP (CLAUDE.md §10).</trigger>
    <trigger>A BFF Redis consumer relies on a command that is not cluster-safe under OSS clustering (multi-key across slots, KEYS on one node, keyspace notifications) → STOP and report; do not change its key design here.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing `Redis-ConnectionString` breaks a consumer other than the stamp BFF (e.g. the Worker's platform vault entry) → STOP; the platform vault entry stays until T242b.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">0 behind origin/master; `/conflict-check`; confirm the inventory (grep `Redis-ConnectionString|redisConnectionString|listKeys|Microsoft.Cache`) → categorized hit list in notes.</step>
    <step order="1">`modules/redis.bicep` → Managed Redis (cluster + database + access-policy assignment; outputs `redisId`, `redisName`, `redisHostName`, `redisPort` = 10000, `redisEndpoint`); parameters sku/highAvailability/principalIds; `redis-{env}.bicepparam` to the new shape; `customer.bicep` passes the UAMI principal, drops the KV secret + connection-string app settings, sets `Redis__Endpoint`; outputs; recompile `customer.json` (`--outfile`); lint.</step>
    <step order="2">Catalog: remove the stamp `Redis-ConnectionString` from-bicep-output entry (keep any platform-scoped entry the Worker needs until T242b); add `Redis__Endpoint` to per_env_settings sourced from H2a; regenerate; H2a → InterStepState → HandlerRunInputs → PerEnvSourceCatalog for the endpoint (Service Bus pattern).</step>
    <step order="3">BFF: packages (StackExchange.Redis ≥ 2.10.1 via `Microsoft.Azure.StackExchangeRedis` 3.3.x; align `Directory.Packages.props`); `RedisOptions.Endpoint`; `CacheModule` Entra branch (async configure, `Protocol = RedisProtocol.Resp3`, same timeouts and AbortOnConnectFail, same `ConnectionMultiplexerFactory` reuse); connection-string branch limited as constrained; startup validation log shows which mode, never a secret; `appsettings.template.json`.</step>
    <step order="4">Worker `DispatchModule`: same endpoint/managed-identity rule for its idempotency cache (`provisioning:` prefix kept); DispatchModuleTests.</step>
    <step order="5">H1 default providers + `Microsoft.Cache`; stale comments; prereqs PRQ-S-03 text; `Rotate-Secrets.ps1` drops customer-scope Redis key rotation; `Decommission-Customer.ps1` uses `sprk-{cid}-{env}-redis` and the redisEnterprise type.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests (scope below); BFF §10 checks; docs + `.claude` (main session) + CHANGELOG.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify: Bicep compiles/lints, JSON = fresh compile; catalog `-Verify`; prereqs validate; BFF builds 0 warnings, BFF unit tests no new failures; ControlPlane 0/0 + tests no failures beyond the T221 baseline; ArchTests pass. Step 9.5 gates. Close + commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

