  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`customer.json` contains a `Microsoft.Cache/redisEnterprise` Balanced_B0 cluster with HA enabled, a database with `accessKeysAuthentication: Disabled`, OSSCluster, AllKeysLRU, and an access-policy assignment for the stamp UAMI principal; it contains no `listKeys`, no `Microsoft.Cache/redis` resource, no `Redis-ConnectionString` secret and no `Redis__ConnectionString` / `ConnectionStrings__Redis` setting; it sets `Redis__Endpoint` and outputs the endpoint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest and every generated file have no stamp `Redis-ConnectionString`; `Redis__Endpoint` flows H2a output → InterStepState → H4b setting; RunContextContractTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF: with `Redis:Endpoint` set, the multiplexer is configured through `ConfigureForAzureWithUserAssignedManagedIdentityAsync(the ManagedIdentity client id)` with RESP3 and no password; with only a connection string in Production the host fails at startup naming `Redis__Endpoint`; in Development/Testing the connection-string and in-memory branches behave as before; with Redis enabled, an endpoint and no managed-identity client id, startup fails naming the missing setting.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Worker `DispatchModule`: same three cases (endpoint → managed identity; connection string only outside Development/Testing → fails; neither → existing fallback rule unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H1 checks `Microsoft.Cache` registration by default; PRQ-S-03 text and validate.ps1 OK.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF §10: Placement Justification in notes; publish size master vs branch (both absolute, delta, zip tool, file counts); no new HIGH CVE; no pre-release package.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Bicep compiles and lints; checked-in JSON = fresh compile (after prettier); BFF build 0 warnings; BFF unit tests and ControlPlane.Tests no failures beyond baseline (T221's 6); ArchTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: CacheModule mode selection (endpoint / connection-string-outside-Development / missing client id), DispatchModule the same, the H2a→H4b endpoint contract, and H1's provider default. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-04 from plan §7 T242 (owner D12, D13), split into T242 (code) and T242b (live dev recreation) because the
    dev per-env cache `spaarke-bff-redis-dev` serves both the dev BFF and the L2 Worker and its recreation is irreversible
    and owner-gated. Inventory: Explore sweep 2026-10-04 (session 34). Researcher recommendation was B1 HA for customers;
    the owner chose B0 HA (D12) — sizing to be confirmed on the first customer's memory metric.

    COMPLETED 2026-10-04 (session 35). Commits `bc73844f9` + gate-fix commit.

    What changed: modules/redis.bicep → Microsoft.Cache/redisEnterprise@2025-07-01 (Balanced_B0, HA param, database
    `default`, accessKeysAuthentication Disabled, OSSCluster, AllKeysLRU, port 10000, access-policy assignments @batchSize(1),
    `accessPolicyPrincipalIds` @minLength(1), outputs incl. `redisEndpoint`); customer.bicep (+json, = fresh compile after
    prettier) — UAMI access policy, `Redis__Endpoint`, no KV secret, params `redisSkuName`/`redisHighAvailability`;
    redis-{dev,staging,prod}.bicepparam (dev: mi-bff-api-dev + sprk-controlplane-dev-uami; staging/prod: non-GUID
    placeholder that blocks deploy — CI compiles every parameters/*.bicepparam, so [] could not be used with minLength);
    catalog (stamp Redis-ConnectionString removed; `Redis__Endpoint` per_env from `from-h2a-output:redis_endpoint`;
    generator allow-list; regenerated, -Verify OK); control plane H2a output → InterStepState.RedisEndpoint → H4b
    (HandlerRunInputs, PerEnvSourceCatalog); Worker DispatchModule; BFF CacheModule/RedisOptions/StartupValidationService/
    template; H1 + Microsoft.Cache; PRQ-S-03; Rotate-Secrets.ps1 (Redis rotation removed); Decommission-Customer.ps1;
    Deploy-RedisCache.ps1 (keyless: redisEnterprise detection, no KV step, -CutoverBffSettings sets Redis__Endpoint and
    leaves ConnectionStrings__Redis for T242b) + tests/manual/RedisValidationTests.ps1; Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1
    (-RedisEndpoint mandatory, host:port pattern) + Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1 (no Redis secret); ADR-009 amended (§6.5
    Path B, owner D12/D13) concise + full; docs + .claude (provisioning.md BINDING section, azure-deployment row, caching
    patterns, secret-catalog pattern, CHANGELOG).

    Deviations (directional steps; recorded): (1) BFF authenticates with `ConfigureForAzureWithTokenCredentialAsync` +
    the shared `ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.Create` (UAMI- and tenant-pinned) instead of
    `ConfigureForAzureWithUserAssignedManagedIdentityAsync(clientId)` — same identity (the configured UAMI; a client id is
    still required, startup fails naming `Graph__ManagedIdentity__ClientId or ManagedIdentity__ClientId`), but ADR-028 A4's
    single shared credential path (adr-check warning). The Worker keeps the clientId API, matching its Cosmos/ServiceBus
    modules' `ManagedIdentity:ClientId` pattern. (2) StackExchange.Redis 2.13.17 (latest 2.x; OTel instrumentation caps
    &lt; 3.0) instead of the 2.10.1 minimum. Its ~160 new IDatabase members broke the hand-written ADR-032 null object →
    `NullDatabase` is now a DispatchProxy with the old contract kept exactly (identity props + inert wait helpers answer,
    every command throws); `RedisScheduledJobLease` passes `keepTtl: false` (2.13 added an Expiration overload a bare
    `expiry:` binds to). (3) Owner 2026-10-04 ("do not defer"): T242b extended — demo cache `spaarke-bff-redis-demo`,
    no-outage dev cut-over (endpoint first; connection string + old cache removed only after master carries T242 +
    INDEX.md note), ordering gates; plus the review follow-ups (Worker module `redisEndpoint`, alerts.bicep resource type,
    live RESP3 / SCAN checks, Seed-PlatformKeyVault, spaarke-resources.yaml). (4) Master-merge fallout fixed:
    `ContactAadObjectIdColumnGuardTests` (from master) flagged L2 systemuser code without a code-level `systemuser` marker
    (IDataverseAppUserCreator record order, T2 probe log text, one test literal).

    Inventory (Step 0) — T242: redis.bicep, customer.bicep/json, manifest + generated, H2a/InterStepState/H4b, H1 options,
    DispatchModule, CacheModule, Rotate-Secrets, Decommission-Customer, prereqs, Configure-ProductionAppSettings,
    Seed-ProductionKeyVault, Deploy-RedisCache (moved here from T242b — the module change broke it), RedisValidationTests.
    T242b (per-env, untouched here): Seed-PlatformKeyVault, controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep + platform json,
    Rotate-RedisKey.ps1, redis-key-rotation.yml, alerts.bicep, config/spaarke-resources.yaml, byok/main.bicep (unchanged),
    vnet.bicep snet-redis (unchanged). Not Redis-owned: remaining customer.json listKeys are Storage/ServiceBus/OpenAI (T244).
    Cluster safety (escalation trigger 3 not fired): both SCAN loops iterate primaries and delete single keys; no multi-key
    commands, Lua, transactions or keyspace notifications outside the null object. Pre-T242 stamps: none (read-only listing
    of all 5 subscriptions 2026-10-04: only spaarke-bff-redis-dev and sprksharedprod-redis [T241]).

    Placement Justification (BFF §10): extends the existing CacheModule registration (auth mode of the BFF's own cache) —
    no new endpoint/service/interface/options class; recorded in design.md §17. Publish (fresh short-path worktrees,
    Compress-Archive, PDBs incl.): master 45.66 MB / 212 files vs branch 45.88 MB / 214 files = +0.22 MB. CVE: none
    (BFF, ControlPlane.Core). No pre-release package added.

    Verification: Bicep build + lint (pre-existing warnings only), customer.json = fresh compile; catalog -Verify OK;
    prereqs validate OK (35); BFF build 0/0; BFF unit suite 14300 total — 14246 passed, 54 skipped, 0 failed (2nd full run, after gate fixes); ControlPlane
    build 0/0, tests 2107/2114 (6 = T221 baseline, 1 skipped); ArchTests 349/349; task-status drift check.
    Step 9.5: code-review (0 Critical, 5 Warning, 11 Suggestion) + adr-check (1 evidence item, 8 warnings) — fixed:
    credential path, null-object contract, client-id message, minLength guard + placeholders, Deploy-RedisCache keyless,
    prod script validation, ADR-009 leftovers (Development/Testing, Standard rationale marked historical, runbook/script
